**Decision (2026-06-12): Gemma is the single routing brain.** The Gemma instance in the xray router stack ([[xray-router]]) owns THREE jobs, all derived from the identity sled / schema state in SHM:
(a) classifies each plugin/mutation into a subid per the taxonomy above;
(b) makes the OpenFlow tag-based routing decision;
(c) resolves subdomains — `*.ghostbridge.tech` → backend mapping becomes part of the xray config Gemma generates dynamically, NOT static dnsmasq/nginx/resolv.conf records. Decoy (129.153.134.63) stays a decoy; Gemma answers internal names to local/wg-xray addresses (split-horizon).
Single source for "what is this," "where does it route," and "what does this name resolve to."

